      "statement": "The source-supported interpretation begins with oxidation of neutral 2a, disfavouring substrate reduction and triplet energy transfer through defined energetic comparisons, and proceeds through connected low-barrier framework rearrangements that favour C4 connectivity over the C5 alternative. The computed endpoint identity and atom/electron balance relate this chemistry to neutral 3a. This is a bounded recovery of the author-calculated activation and rearrangement findings, not proof of a unique or fully calculated photocatalytic cycle.",
      "expected": "The source-supported interpretation begins with oxidation of neutral 2a, disfavouring substrate reduction and triplet energy transfer through defined energetic comparisons, and proceeds through connected low-barrier framework rearrangements that favour C4 connectivity over the C5 alternative. The computed endpoint identity and atom/electron balance relate this chemistry to neutral 3a. This is a bounded recovery of the author-calculated activation and rearrangement findings, not proof of a unique or fully calculated photocatalytic cycle. Award credit only for the stated source-supported scientific finding established by genuine linked computation. Resolve submitted model/result/claim/operation/artifact IDs, molecular graphs, charge/spin, units, reference states and conditions. A claimed minimum or saddle needs appropriate frequency/state evidence, and any mechanistic connection needs an IRC or scientifically equivalent endpoint/connection test. Normal termination, source coordinates, value proximity, copied numbers and unsupported labels alone are insufficient. Independently valid components retain their own credit; missing, opposite or unresolved results earn zero for that finding. Honest failure, search coverage and ordinary limitations are assessed on the process axis and have no standalone scientific points. Methods and labels are open; the source-supported physical result must still be recovered. Do not impose a unique global mechanism when the source only supports the scoped model. New numerical tolerances may not be inferred from source values or from old verification failures. Reagent reference data are not substrate calculations. Separate author computations, experiments and mechanistic proposals. Integrate the scored findings without duplicate scientific points.",
